src/nist_sp_800_53/schema/*.yaml, src/nist_sp_800_53/datamodel/ and
project/ model the security and privacy controls that the National
Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) defines in Special
Publication (SP) 800-53, Revision 5, https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-53r5
(September 2020, updated December 2020; Release 5.2.0 of August 2025),
with the assessment procedures of SP 800-53A, Revision 5,
https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-53Ar5, and the control baselines of
SP 800-53B, https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-53B. They are this
project's rendering, written in its own words with NIST as the source of
the definitions; they are not NIST's, and their use does not imply
endorsement by NIST.

The three publications are works of the United States Government and
are not subject to copyright in the United States. NIST's statement on
its works, read on 2026-10-29 at
https://www.nist.gov/open/copyright-fair-use-and-licensing-statements-srd-data-software-and-technical-series-publications,
adds that such a work may be subject to copyright in other countries.

Third-party test data
---------------------

tests/data/third-party/nist/ holds copies of NIST's catalog of SP 800-53
Revision 5, its baseline profiles and resolved catalogs, the Revision 4
baseline profiles and OSCAL's example documents, in the Open Security
Controls Assessment Language (OSCAL), retrieved from
https://github.com/usnistgov/oscal-content, beside NIST's LICENSE.md from
that repository. NIST's work is in the public domain within the United
States, and NIST dedicates it to the worldwide public domain under CC0
1.0. tests/data/third-party/cprt/ holds three exports of the same release
from NIST's Cybersecurity and Privacy Reference Tool, on the same terms.

tests/data/third-party/hyperGRC/ holds OSCAL-shaped fixtures derived from
the agencyapp example of GovReady's hyperGRC,
https://github.com/GovReady/hyperGRC/tree/master/example/agencyapp, which
is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3, as the
LICENSE.md beside them records. The tests read them; nothing in this
repository redistributes hyperGRC's code.

